{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons","id":1509262,"title":"Solar-Circle Exigent Sorcerer Patrons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-22T01:25:49-07:00","id":1509262,"title":"Solar-Circle Exigent Sorcerer Patrons","content":"Solar-Circle Sorcerers are supposed to be vanishingly rare. For the published Exigent types, most are Terrestrial-Circle with a few tricks or exceptions to allow them access to Celestial-Circle, and no published ones can go higher. What would be a good patron for an Exigent who can natively access the Solar-Circle at the appropriate Essence-tier?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the God of Geomancy, on the grounds of being in-tune with the Essence of all Creation, but it's far from perfect.<br /> <br /> Five Days Darkness would also be an interesting option, since he's Sol Invictus' shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T07:23:42-07:00","id":1509274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons#post1509262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar-Circle Sorcerers are supposed to be vanishingly rare. For the published Exigent types, most are Terrestrial-Circle with a few tricks or exceptions to allow them access to Celestial-Circle, and no published ones can go higher. What would be a good patron for an Exigent who can natively access the Solar-Circle at the appropriate Essence-tier?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the God of Geomancy, on the grounds of being in-tune with the Essence of all Creation, but it's far from perfect.<br /> <br /> Five Days Darkness would also be an interesting option, since he's Sol Invictus' shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, Five Days Darkness being the shadow of the UCS is one of the quite few beings who feels &quot;right&quot; for such a thing, since the Adamant Circle is pretty much the sun's purview (except maybe for the Yozis and their <i>Fetiches</i>, perhaps).<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, Adamant Circle is such a vanishingly niche and rare thing in the already rarefied field that is <b>any</b> Sorcery above the Emerald Circle i would be tempted to make acquiring it a matter of sorcerous quests/uplifting/workings than looking for any sort of patron. But that's just my personal opinion and preferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T23:10:33-07:00","id":1509351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509274#post1509274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Five Days Darkness being the shadow of the UCS is one of the quite few beings who feels &quot;right&quot; for such a thing, since the Adamant Circle is pretty much the sun's purview (except maybe for the Yozis and their <i>Fetiches</i>, perhaps).</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangentially related then - what would FDD's Exigent look like?<br /> <br /> <b><i>Chosen of Strange Days</i></b><br /> <i>Celestial Tier. Adamant Sorcerery, Sidereal Martial Arts</i><br /> <b>Themes</b>:<ul><li><u>Calibration</u>, and the weirdness inherent to those five days. Anarchy? Deviation from the norm? Chaos in a non-Wyld sense?</li> <li><u>Shadows</u>, in the sense of those we cast rather than the absence-of-light opposition of The Ebon Dragon. The silhouette of a person, as opposed to their dark reflection</li> <li><u>Secrets</u>, since he has dominion over things in darkness. 2e gave him a charm to that effect.</li> <li><u>Vengeance</u>? He's got that semi-petty thing with the Calendar Spirits</li> <li><u>Loyalty</u>? He's loyal to Creation, and to the Unconquered Sun despite being perpetually banished from his presence</li> </ul><b>Caste Abilities</b><ul><li><u>Martial Arts</u>, since FDD is an Immaculate Grandmaster</li> <li><u>Occult</u>, for secrets &quot;untouched by the light of day&quot;</li> <li><u>Dodge</u>? He dodges the sun every day</li> <li><u>Stealth/Larceny</u>? He's a goddamn shapeshifting shadow</li> <li><u>Investigation</u>? Going back to the 2e &quot;secrets untouched by the light of day&quot; charm</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-23-2023, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T12:38:17-07:00","id":1509405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509274#post1509274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, Five Days Darkness being the shadow of the UCS is one of the quite few beings who feels &quot;right&quot; for such a thing, since the Adamant Circle is pretty much the sun's purview</div> </div> </div> </div>Charting Fate's Course establishes that even the Incarnae are apparently not capable of Solar Circle Sorcery. Essence 9+ gods who are master sorcerers can have access to a single spell appropriate to their nature at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(except maybe for the Yozis and their <i>Fetiches</i>, perhaps).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this Edition establishes any particular relationship between Yozis and sorcery, and given how sorcery is being a bit more firmly established as &quot;thing done by people who come across as sorcerers&quot;, I'd see they're even further removed from it (even as I largely assume that the Yozi form of power is expansive enough to render casting spells largely redundant).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T00:34:42-07:00","id":1509458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509405#post1509405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Charting Fate's Course establishes that even the Incarnae are apparently not capable of Solar Circle Sorcery. Essence 9+ gods who are master sorcerers can have access to a single spell appropriate to their nature at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but the Chosen of one of the Incarnae totally have Solar Circle Sorcery. I suppose that's a good argument for severely <i>broadening </i>the limits of what kinds of Exigents can attain the Circle of Adamant, since it gaining it seems unrelated to the exact capabilities of their patron.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509405#post1509405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this Edition establishes any particular relationship between Yozis and sorcery, and given how sorcery is being a bit more firmly established as &quot;thing done by people who come across as sorcerers&quot;, I'd see they're even further removed from it (even as I largely assume that the Yozi form of power is expansive enough to render casting spells largely redundant).</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see if Paths of Brigid (if it ever gets written) changes the story of how Brigid learned sorcery at the feet of a demoness. Regardless, though, we've still got indications that spells like Total Annihilation exist in this edition, so it seems clear that beings like Ligier can help provide the scaffolding on which Adamant Circle Spells are cast. Maybe in this vein you could have an Exigent who is partly empowered by a being like Orabilis, or Ligier, or a similarly potent Demon, that uses the strange infusion of hellish power to reach to the heights of the Adamant Circle. Sounds like it could make for a very fun character concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T01:25:23-07:00","id":1509460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509458#post1509458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but the Chosen of one of the Incarnae totally have Solar Circle Sorcery. I suppose that's a good argument for severely <i>broadening </i>the limits of what kinds of Exigents can attain the Circle of Adamant, since it gaining it seems unrelated to the exact capabilities of their patron.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't quite call it unrelated. The Unconquered Sun embodies a kind of boundless excellence, but still expressed in the manner of a god, where there's a necessary focus and structure to it. When that becomes a quality for Exalted humans, who are less immediately powerful but have a certain broader flexibility, that becomes something that can specifically reach certain heights or break certain boundaries.<br /> <br /> There are Exigents who can uncommonly and unpredictably come out with power comparable to that of a Solar, but they're still tied to their own themes; Strawmaiden Janest brings a lot of force, but it's force backing up the legend of the empowered farm girl.<br /> <br /> I think it would make the most sense for a comparable Exigent who can get in on Solar Circle Sorcery to come from a god whose purview is weird and esoteric, something kind of ethereal so that if they turn out to be the strongest type of Exigent it's pointed at something that can touch off of the strangest magic.<br /> <br /> Although still ultimately a bit of a theoretical idea; there's always the issue that it would take Essence 5 to get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll see if Paths of Brigid (if it ever gets written) changes the story of how Brigid learned sorcery at the feet of a demoness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mara is in the core book, she's still a sorcerous and can teach sorcery to others.<br /> <br /> That in itself does not need to have anything to do with the power of the Yozis, and indeed, I think later Second Edition opting to recontextualize Brigid's narrative into an implication that sorcery was a trap laid for her by Yozis actually did the character of Mara a disservice. It took the heat of her own persona and qualities and handed it over to the Yozis, who had plenty enough as it was.<br /> <br /> It also really weakened the origin of sorcery narrative because when people got it into their heads that it was something handed over by the Yozis through a proxy, by virtue of being a specifically Primordial thing, it made them forget the fact that there were several other important supernatural figures in that narrative teaching Brigid as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, though, we've still got indications that spells like Total Annihilation exist in this edition, so it seems clear that beings like Ligier can help provide the scaffolding on which Adamant Circle Spells are cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Solar Circle Sorcery require a demon's assistance to such some power from it and channel it into something to make it explode? There's a Solar Circle spell to make a desert bloom, but that doesn't mean flowers have anything to do with the pinnacle of sorcerous power.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T19:28:48-07:00","id":1509544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509405#post1509405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Charting Fate's Course establishes that even the Incarnae are apparently not capable of Solar Circle Sorcery. Essence 9+ gods who are master sorcerers can have access to a single spell appropriate to their nature at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Immaterial - when i framed the &quot;<i>maybe </i>appropriate&quot; for Five Days Darkness was from the perspective of him <i>as the shadow of the Unconquered Sun</i>, no more, no less.<br /> I'm pretty certain i said &quot;<b>beings</b>&quot;, <b>not </b>gods, elementals or Incarnae.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509405#post1509405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this Edition establishes any particular relationship between Yozis and sorcery, and given how sorcery is being a bit more firmly established as &quot;thing done by people who come across as sorcerers&quot;, I'd see they're even further removed from it (even as I largely assume that the Yozi form of power is expansive enough to render casting spells largely redundant).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's <b>a lot</b> this Edition has not established yet, so most of us fill the dots with bits and parts from previous ones that still stick to our minds (or deconstruct them on purpose when in a contrarian mood, but i digress) - but Mara is still around, some form of Infernal Exalted will still be around and Dukantha had all 3 circles of Sorcery even in first edition. So i'm quite comfortable with the idea of <b><i>those who were once Primordials</i></b> having access to it and their Fetich souls having <i>limited access to particular spells where thematically appropriate</i>, even if just personal preference.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T02:56:46-07:00","id":1509567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509544#post1509544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Immaterial - when i framed the &quot;<i>maybe </i>appropriate&quot; for Five Days Darkness was from the perspective of him <i>as the shadow of the Unconquered Sun</i>, no more, no less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what about that is a basis for him being a Solar Circle Sorcerer?<br /> <br /> If Five Days Darkness isn't a god, then he can't use the Exigence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's <b>a lot</b> this Edition has not established yet, so most of us fill the dots with bits and parts from previous ones that still stick to our minds (or deconstruct them on purpose when in a contrarian mood, but i digress)\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think the only reason a person would propose, say, that the origin of the Dragon-Blooded did not involve them being in a big orgy to keep the women constantly pregnant as quickly as possible was because that person was contrarian? <br /> <br /> Before we got a full proper write-up for Ma-Ha-Suchi I would challenge people who brought in an assumption that he still had rape camps, did I have no more sophisticated reason to do that than being contrarian?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T05:59:03-07:00","id":1509576,"title":"","content":"Which Gods have Solar Circle Sorcery?<br /> 'Which Gods have purviews that are related to Sorcery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:45:23-07:00","id":1509620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509460#post1509460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would make the most sense for a comparable Exigent who can get in on Solar Circle Sorcery to come from a god whose purview is weird and esoteric, something kind of ethereal so that if they turn out to be the strongest type of Exigent it's pointed at something that can touch off of the strangest magic.<br /> <br /> Although still ultimately a bit of a theoretical idea; there's always the issue that it would take Essence 5 to get.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the interest of having a constructive conversation, what kinds of purviews do you think would be fitting for such gods? A few of the suggestions I've seen include:<ul><li>A god of a constellation within the House of Secrets.</li> <li>A god of astrology, generally.</li> <li>A god of a specific category of secret knowledge.</li> <li>A god of research or invention.</li> <li>A god whose domain, whatever it was, was declared secret and has had to hide their existence since then.</li> <li>A god of libraries, or a specific incredibly famous library of sorcerous knowledge.</li> <li>A god tied to an incredible potent sorcerous artifact, akin to the Book of Three Circles or the like.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509262-solar-circle-exigent-sorcerer-patrons?p=1509460#post1509460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Solar Circle Sorcery require a demon's assistance to such some power from it and channel it into something to make it explode? There's a Solar Circle spell to make a desert bloom, but that doesn't mean flowers have anything to do with the pinnacle of sorcerous power.</div> </div> </div> </div>No? And your rhetorical question doesn't actually have anything to do with what I said. Sorcery in Exalted has always arisen from in-setting places, throughout the game's history. Animal Avatars, the Eyeless Face, the Unconquered Sun, the Five Maidens, even Gaia are described in the writeups of Solar Circle Spells, in various ways. It's part of what gives Sorcery its unique and recognizable texture. Seems weird to throw that out just to argue that Ligier is somehow unsuited to be a granter of sorcerous power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:57:43-07:00","id":1509623,"title":"","content":"My offerings would be (of varying quality and justification):<ul><li>God of Geomancy, on the grounds of being in-tune with the Essence of all Creation</li> <li>Five Days Darkness, on the grounds of being the Sun's shadow. For that matter, any of his children, be it Little Beam, Nysela, or Ardis-Iara.</li> <li>A god of boundaries and/or transgressions, on the grounds of breaking established limitations (though that steps on Autocthon's toes a bit as a purview)</li> <li>The god of Thaumaturgy (can't remember his name) on the grounds of Thaumaturgy being the weird (and underpowered for cost) glitches in the fabric of Creation</li> <li>Wyld-tainted gods, on the grounds that the Wyld is the raw fabric ito which Creation is woven</li> <li>Gods of creativity/creation, on the grounds that Sorcery is often a way to make something whole new (and a generous helping of 2e's &quot;Sorcery is the source code of Creation)</li> <li>Gods of turning points or paradigm shifts, on the grounds of Sorcery often pulling a rabbit out of the hat.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}